[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]Cmd: help
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display: Console Help:
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display: =============
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display:  
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display: A console variable is a engine wide key value pair. The key is a string usually starting with the subsystem prefix followed
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display: by '.' e.g. r.BloomQuality. The value can be of different tpe (e.g. float, int, string). A console command has no state associated with
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display: and gets executed immediately.
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display:  
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display: Console variables can be put into ini files (e.g. ConsoleVariables.ini or BaseEngine.ini) with this syntax:
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display: <Console variable> = <value>
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display:  
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display: DumpConsoleCommands         Lists all console variables and commands that are registered (Some are not registered)
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display: <Console variable>          Get the console variable state
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display: <Console variable> ?        Get the console variable help text
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display: <Console variable> <value>  Set the console variable value
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display: <Console command> [Params]  Execute the console command with optional parameters
[2025.04.02-10.15.15:012][114]LogEngine: Display:  
